11.0.0, nineteenth upload — Field over your video, Jam with nearby iPhones, tempo to the hundredth

What is new since 10027. Each line is code that the Echoel Studio run builds and, where a test
target reaches it, tests; nothing here is device-verified yet.
- Field over Video: Export Video has Field Layer (Off, Screen, Add, Normal) and Field Opacity;
  the Field is drawn over your video take in every frame shape, vertical too. The video window
  previews the same picture. Two exports of the same song draw the same film; body values are
  not part of an export.
- Jam: Song menu, Connect, Jam…. Host a Jam or Join a Jam; nearby iPhones follow the host's
  tempo, time signature and Play/Stop, directly and encrypted, without Wi-Fi or internet. Only
  timing and device names travel, no sound and no body values. Off until you host or join.
- Tempo to the hundredth: type 100,25; the transport shows only the places it needs
  (120, 100,5, 100,25).

Previous: 11.0.0 (10027), eighteenth upload — the identity finished. 10025 and earlier: see
git history of this file.
group.com.echoelmusic (the import of earlier songs) is still not requested (F17).

Bump this file on a commit whose "Echoel Studio" run is green to upload a build
(.github/workflows/studio-testflight.yml). Build number = 10000 + the workflow's run number.
The version is MARKETING_VERSION in EchoelStudio/project.yml.
This file is a test list for the device, not a source for claims (ContentPipeline/CLAIMS.md).

Five things to try on the device (FOUNDER_INBOX rule 1: five per build; answer each yes or no):
1. Type 100,25 as the tempo on the number pad: the transport shows 100,25 BPM and the click
   follows it.
2. A camera take, Field Layer Screen at 60 %: the video window shows the Field over you.
3. Export Video, 9:16, about 30 s, with that layer: the Field sits upright over you and pulses
   with the beat; does Screen look right to your eye, or too bright in the mid tones?
4. Two iPhones, Wi-Fi off: one hosts at 100,25 BPM with the click on, the other joins; it comes
   in on the next bar and both clicks sound together, still after five minutes.
5. Put the host in airplane mode: the other shows "Jam host lost. Playing on at 100,25 BPM."
   and keeps playing.
